Chapter: SpikePondMain
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Sky
  cites Poc chapter Spike
  cites Poc chapter SpikePrint

 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. The duck pond and the zebras, split off `SpikeMain`.

 THE SPLIT IS CONVENIENCE NOW, NOT NECESSITY. It was made when two viewpoints was
 all the QEMU guest's heap would hold; since the printers stopped concatenating
 left to right (PORTING_NOTES C17) an entry peaks at 133 MB and all eight would fit
 in one binary. The pairs are kept because they already exist and because the third
 arm runs one entry at a time, so a failure names two viewpoints rather than
 eight.

 Named for the pond because that is what the first viewpoint looks at; the zebras
 ride along because they are the next viewpoint down the route and a pair is the
 unit here.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (scene-line "duck-pond" u-pond)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-pond) 0)
    print-line-uni (scene-line "zebras" u-zebras)
    print-line-uni (all-cmds (spike-frame-at u-zebras) 0)
  end
